  "notes": "Backlog game, all-AAA pass: picked from RAWG's most-added list for its year across all genres (docs/PLAN.md section 2, genre filter widened 2026-10-23). Steam app 640590. StrategyWiki has no page under \"The LEGO Ninjago Movie Video Game\"; the alternative \"The Lego Ninjago Movie Video Game\" redirects to \"The LEGO Ninjago Movie Videogame\", a stub page (completion stage 0) that links Walkthrough, Gameplay and Table of Contents subpages, none of them written, so nothing was used. lego.fandom.com has a \"The LEGO Ninjago Movie Video Game\" page with about 66 linked pages; names only were looked at, nothing copied. None of the 50 Steam achievements is hidden. The story is split into two chapters by the location numbers the achievements give (Location 1 to 8). \"Master of Destruction\" (destroy Ninjago City) sits with the later locations. RAWG average playtime is 1 hour, which looks too low for a full game."
